// Checkpoint' spec (Q11)", rows "Checkpoint record" .. "Post-intro checkpoint") ----
// (1) chapter.cp <unit> <checkpoint id> ("Chapter from checkpoint"): Lara at a chosen checkpoint through the game's own
//     checkpoint restart, no intro. The checkpoints come from the game data at run time (truintro::ScanCheckpoints, a
//     background read of mods\<unit>.drm / patch.000 / bigfile.000 10 s after the intro table: every placed intro of
//     the objects checkpoint / invis_checkpoint / dlc2_checkpoint / checkpoint_l1_going_in / _out, ids from the game's
//     object list; offline selftest TruCpScanTest = tools/unit_checkpoint_table.py, 303 / 303) - no local table needed.
//     Gate (game thread): 20 byte checks kCcChecks + kCrChecks, experimental, main state 1, a player, no cutscene, no
//     level change, restart bit 0x80000 clear, pause bit not the game's, both game blocks version 0x0c2c and word +0x1f4
//     = 0 (else the alternative record is used), unit in the level list with a DRM, the K1 reload guard of 0.22.67 (a
//     live costume switch: the restart would birth the checkpoint costume), no DLC change (Lara's unit group = the
//     target's: base game / DLC 1 / DLC 2), the id is a checkpoint of the unit (run-time table, or a loaded instance
//     with object word [[inst+0x50]+8] 0xb / 0xc). Then save.backup kapitel and:
//       loaded target with its instance: INSTANCE_Post(inst, 0x196, 1) (synchronous: 0x5b3750 calls [inst+0x120] at
//         once) = the game's own set + snapshot; the tracker / live / snapshot records must name (unit, id), else stop;
//       else (unit not loaded, or no instance): the record (unit[128], id) written into the snapshot game block
//         [0xc59268], the live one [0xc59264] and the player tracker [0xfadb58]+0x648 / +0x6c8, read back;
//     then the restart request of cp.reload ([0xe7f0b8] |= 0x80000): the record's unit loaded -> in place 0x5de480,
//     else the full reload 0x5df760(6) into the snapshot state, placement 0x5d40c0 on the record checkpoint. During main
//     state 2 the played marks of the level-start intros (table of 0.22.66) of the target's level group are kept at 1
//     (the target unit's own intro included) - as after a death; for 10 s after the landing the record is watched (the
//     post-intro branch 11733 sets 4302 by itself) and set back once with 0x196(1) when it moved off the target.
// (2) sonar.cplabels ("Sonar: checkpoint labels"), default off: in the PDA sonar the checkpoints of map units that the
//     sonar loaded only as a map (no instances) are labelled from the run-time table. Place = data position - Level+0x80
//     (FinishLoad 0x5d1cd0) + the sonar unit's own shift +0xa0 (0x6dde00 adds every placing offset there, to the mesh
//     origins and the portals, and sets +0xb3 = 1). Not proven before: on every open the same formula is checked on the
//     loaded units' checkpoint instances (live positions) - the labels are drawn only when every compared checkpoint is
//     within 100 units ("proven" in the log line), else the header says why and nothing is drawn.
